# graphify
- **graphify** (`~/.claude/skills/graphify/SKILL.md`) - any input to knowledge graph. Trigger: `/graphify`
When the user types `/graphify`, use the installed graphify skill or instructions before doing anything else.

# gstack
Use the `/browse` skill from gstack (`~/.claude/skills/gstack`) for all web browsing. Never use `mcp__claude-in-chrome__*` tools.

Available gstack skills: `/office-hours`, `/plan-ceo-review`, `/plan-eng-review`, `/plan-design-review`, `/design-consultation`, `/design-shotgun`, `/design-html`, `/review`, `/ship`, `/land-and-deploy`, `/canary`, `/benchmark`, `/browse`, `/connect-chrome`, `/qa`, `/qa-only`, `/design-review`, `/setup-browser-cookies`, `/setup-deploy`, `/setup-gbrain`, `/retro`, `/investigate`, `/document-release`, `/document-generate`, `/codex`, `/cso`, `/autoplan`, `/plan-devex-review`, `/devex-review`, `/careful`, `/freeze`, `/guard`, `/unfreeze`, `/gstack-upgrade`, `/learn`.

# Security reviews
Whenever the user asks to add or check "seguridad"/security on any project, use the `security-review` skill (and the `security-guidance`/`security-scan` plugins where relevant) before finishing the task.

# ruflo
`ruflo-core` (plugin `ruflo-core@ruflo`, from https://github.com/ruvnet/ruflo) is installed and available — prefer it for multi-agent orchestration/efficiency on coding projects when its approach fits the task. Note: only `ruflo-core` was installed, not the full ruflo ecosystem (37 sub-plugins). Deliberately excluded: `ruflo-neural-trader` and `ruflo-market-data`, whose bundled `agent-trading-predictor` skill instructs executing real financial trades — this conflicts with the standing rule to never execute financial trades, so it is not installed and should not be added without the user revisiting that decision explicitly.
